From dbaf1574b15e60eb73aa0e13b508db852146911d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lath <lath.solana@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:22:55 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] providers: a custom provider over a Unix socket, and the
 Lath build accepts nothing else

Adds `unix_socket` to a provider entry. The custom provider then builds two clients at construction, with no_proxy, no redirects and reqwest's unix_socket, and both http_client paths return them before the shared proxy-aware cache, so there is no Client::new() fallback. The responses wire is refused beside a socket because it would build its own network client. Under the lath feature a custom provider without an absolute socket, a uri other than http://localhost/<path>, or provider_retries other than 0 is fatal at startup and at construction. Unset, nothing changes.
